# Input: cargo-about 0.8.2's locked, target-filtered JSON output.
# @html escapes all dependency-supplied strings and full license text.
def html: tostring | @html;
"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width\"><title>WSDist third-party notices</title><style>body{max-width:75rem;margin:2rem auto;padding:0 1rem;font-family:sans-serif}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}td,th{padding:.4rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}table{border-collapse:collapse}tr{border-bottom:1px solid #aaa}</style></head><body>\n<h1>WSDist third-party software notices</h1>\n<p>Generated from the locked application graph with cargo-about 0.8.2. Build dependencies are included as a conservative superset of the delivered code. Crate expressions below are upstream declarations, not a license grant for WSDist code, game data or icons. <a href=\"PROVENANCE.txt\">Provenance and licensing boundaries</a>.</p>\n<p>For OR expressions the policy prefers MIT, then Apache-2.0. All required AND terms are retained. Slint 1.16.0 uses <a href=\"licenses/Slint-Royalty-free-2.0.txt\">Slint Royalty-free Applications License 2.0</a>, with its AboutSlint widget available in the top-level Help menu. Cargo-about cannot render custom LicenseRef text, so that full text is supplied separately.</p>\n<p><a href=\"licenses/Slint-asset-attributions.txt\">Slint artwork/font attributions</a> include the <a href=\"licenses/crates/i-slint-compiler-1.16.0/LICENSES/CC-BY-ND-4.0.txt\">AboutSlint logo license</a> and <a href=\"licenses/OFL-1.1-RFN.txt\">Inter font license</a>. <a href=\"licenses/Rust-standard-library.html\">Rust 1.92.0 standard-library notices</a> are preserved separately. Original crate notices and any alternative license documents are in <code>licenses/crates/</code>.</p>\n<h2>Resolved third-party crates and exact source</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Crate</th><th>Version</th><th>Declared license expression</th><th>Source archive</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n"
+ ([.crates[] | "<tr><td><a href=\"" + ((.package.repository // ("https://crates.io/crates/" + .package.name)) | html) + "\">" + (.package.name | html) + "</a></td><td>" + (.package.version | html) + "</td><td>" + ((.package.license // .license) | html) + "</td><td><a href=\"https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/" + (.package.name | html) + "/" + (.package.version | html) + "/download\">Released source</a></td></tr>"] | join("\n"))
+ "\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>Selected standard license texts and upstream copyright notices</h2>\n"
+ ([.licenses[] | "<section><h3>" + (.name | html) + " (" + (.id | html) + ")</h3><p>Used by: " + ([.used_by[] | (.crate.name + " " + .crate.version) | html] | join(", ")) + "</p><pre>" + (.text | html) + "</pre></section>"] | join("\n"))
+ "\n</body></html>\n"
